# interplay_memlive_held_unmap: An exec that fills a live shared buffer S and a shared buffer N no exec has named waits on the gate while the worker FIFO unmaps (34) both pages. In the blocks setup the unmap calls the host's unmap_memory, which replaces the host task's pages at those VAs; in the map setup and in the service it only unmaps object lists that overlap (docs/testing.md section 6.10). Released, S fills the pages it was made over and N is made (in the blocks setup the range tracker maps its page again). A MapMemory2 (57) on the worker, and fills through both again, follow. Every fill lands in the guest pages in every setup: the blocks setup's Metal buffer over S keeps the guest page it was made over after the host task's VA is replaced.
